</code> 
This is related to the comment "// @@@ the array contains the value being returned" in Add function. Returns the value that added to the end i.e. the added value must be equal to the value which returned. We use a Debug.Assert to check this condition holds true or not.

<code>
Debug.Assert(_size == 0);
</code> 
This is related to the comment "// @@@ Count returns 0 if ArrayList is Empty" in Clear function. Clear method makes size 0 when all elements delete, so it checks the size is equal to 0. We use a Debug.Assert to check this condition.

<code>
Debug.Assert(index == -1 || _items[index] == value);
</code> 
This is related to the comment "// @@@ the ArrayList contains the value after call Remove()" in Remove function. Removing a value from an ArrayList will decrease the size by 1, so it checks whether the value that was removed still exists in the list. The index must be equal to -1 or the value at the specified index is equal to the removed value. If the value does not exist in the ArrayList, it returns -1. We use a Debug.Assert to check this condition.

<code>
