This is related to the comment "// @@@ Returns the index of the last occurrence of a given value in a range of this list" in LastIndexOf function. This function will return -1 when the element does not exist in ArrayList or when it is in greater index than specified index 'index', so it checks index either equal to -1 or greater than 'index' for the value. We use a Debug.Assert to check this condition holds true or not.

<code>
