The output represents an assertion that is related to the state of the data structure at various points in the code. Thus, it checks that the array has the original capacity at the start, that the count is correct after the operations performed, that the value at the index matches the expected value after the operation, etc. The code is meant to catch bugs or incorrect assumptions that might cause an ArrayOutOfBoundException in some cases, or other issues, that could lead to undesired behavior or undefined behavior. These debug assertions can thus help catch such issues, thus reducing the chances of a crash and improving the robustness of the code.--------------------
